[20.732277, "o", "ð¬ Claude: Here's a demonstration of the Go code:\r\r\n\r\r\n```go\r\r\npackage main\r\r\n\r\r\nimport (\r\r\n\t\"fmt\"\r\r\n\t\"io\"\r\r\n\t\"os\"\r\r\n\r\r\n\t\"golang.org/x/crypto/sha3\"\r\r\n)\r\r\n\r\r\nfunc main() {\r\r\n\tif len(os.Args) < 2 {\r\r\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"usage: keccak <file>\")\r\r\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\r\r\n\t}\r\r\n\r\r\n\tf, err := os.Open(os.Args[1])\r\r\n\tif err != nil {\r\r\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, err)\r\r\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\r\r\n\t}\r\r\n\tdefer f.Close()\r\r\n\r\r\n\th := sha3.NewLegacyKeccak256()\r\r\n\tif _, err := io.Copy(h, f); err != nil {\r\r\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, err)\r\r\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\r\r\n\t}\r\r\n\r\r\n\tfmt.Printf(\"%x\\n\", h.Sum(nil))\r\r\n}\r\r\n```\r\r\n\r\r\n**Key points:**\r\r\n- Uses `sha3.NewLegacyKeccak256()` for true Keccak-256 (Ethereum-compatible), not `sha3.New256()` which is SHA3-256\r\r\n- `io.Copy` streams the file without loading it entirely into memory\r\r\n- Outputs lowercase hex hash to stdout\r\r\n"]
